  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (PCA, single profile) achieves 48.5% accuracy while image (ResNet50) is very weak at 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant signal. PCA is a simple linear projection and likely underperforms learned encoders on single-cell data. Question: Does replacing PCA with a learned variational encoder (scvi_n200) improve RNA representation quality and validation accuracy? This experiment changes only the RNA encoder while keeping single-profile and no aggregation fixed, cleanly isolating the encoder effect. Rationale: With 7 experiments remaining, establishing whether a learned encoder beats PCA is the highest-value uncertainty to resolve. If scvi substantially improves over 48.5%, it justifies investing remaining budget in scvi-based multimodal or multiprofile configurations; if not, PCA is sufficient and we should pivot to aggregation/fusion strategies. This is a minimal, single-variable change from the best-performing config so far."
}

